# String.push scalar-overload dispatch.
#
# `String.push(x)` must route to the typed runtime variant chosen by the LIR
# type of the value argument:
#   bool  → gorget_string_push_bool
#   int   → gorget_string_push_int
#   float → gorget_string_push_float
#   Str   → gorget_string_push_char  (the Str-ABI fall-through)
#
# Before the dispatch fix the self-host lowerer routed EVERY `push` to the
# Str-ABI `gorget_string_push_char`, so a scalar arg got zeroed to `(Str){0}`
# and silently vanished. Each scalar line below would print the wrong (empty)
# chunk. The C backend and the self-host lowerer must agree byte-for-byte.
#
# (push_line is intentionally NOT exercised here: the self-host frontend still
# lowers String.push_line with a value-returning destination — a separate gap,
# see TODO — so it cannot yet round-trip end-to-end in the self-host. The LIR
# dispatch at lir_lower.gg DOES cover push_line for when that gap is fixed.)

void main():
    String s = ""
    s.push(42)
    s.push(" ")
    s.push(3.5)
    s.push(" ")
    s.push(true)
    s.push(" ")
    s.push(false)
    s.push(" ")
    s.push("done")
    print(s)
